+
+## Keyword search in Sigma rules
+
+Sigma detections can search for a word without naming an event field:
+
+```yaml
+detection:
+  keywords:
+    - suspicious command
+  condition: keywords
+```
+
+When a loaded rule or correlation needs keyword search, Zircolite captures the
+original decoded event values during ingestion and stores them in its private
+`_sigma_fulltext` column. It walks object keys in sorted order and array items in
+source order, writing scalar values on separate lines. This happens before field
+mappings, exclusions, transforms, flattening and generated metadata, so a word
+in an excluded or transformed source value can still match. Empty events store
+an empty string. The search text is omitted from matches, correlation evidence,
+CSV/JSON output and `--keepflat` exports. It is not indexed by `--auto-index`.
+
+Rules converted by this version carry `schema_version: 3` and a `fulltext`
+requirement when they need that column. Correlation plans that depend on such
+rules use version 3. Existing rules and plans remain version 2. A saved database
+retains the text and its `_zircolite_fulltext` provenance table. Databases made
+before this feature must be **re-ingested** to run keyword-dependent rules;
+Zircolite reports those rules as unevaluable while continuing independent
+rules. Adding a column manually to an old database does not reconstruct the
+original values. A source field or mapping named `_sigma_fulltext` is rejected
+when capture is enabled.
+
+Library users can capture before rules are loaded by passing
+`ProcessingConfig(fulltext_capture=True)` to `ZircoliteCore` or
+`StreamingEventProcessor`. Loading rules with `core.load_ruleset_from_var(...)`
+before `core.run_streaming(...)` also enables capture. The command-line
+processing modes derive this setting from the loaded rules automatically.
